# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# pfmatch
#
# The working tree is ~6.9 GB; the package is ~1.1 MB. Everything large here is
# either a public source file that can be re-downloaded or a derived artifact
# that regenerates from inputs/ plus the BMF. What IS tracked is the code, the
# small public fixtures, and the hand-adjudicated ground truth -- that last one
# cannot be regenerated at any price.
#
# Note the `dir/*` form rather than `dir/`: git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the negations below only work this way.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- derived artifacts, caches, checkpoints (6.3 GB) ----------------------
data-dev/*
# ... except the audit samples the verdicts in dev/maybe-verdicts.csv key to
!data-dev/AUDIT-MAYBE-100.csv
!data-dev/AUDIT-NO-100.csv
!data-dev/AUDIT-NO-100-PROBE.csv
!data-dev/AUDIT-OOS-100.csv

# ... and the ground truth, which the header above already says is tracked and
# which these rules did not in fact cover. Hand adjudication is the one thing
# here that cannot be regenerated from inputs/ plus the BMF at any price, and
# until 2026-10-23 all of it lived only in a Dropbox folder. ~7 MB in total.
!data-dev/PF-TRUTH.csv
!data-dev/PF-TRUTH-V2.csv
!data-dev/LIFT-CROSSWALK-V2.csv

# ... and the address-triangulation set: 2,853 informative cases over 4,326
# address groups, where one organisation is written several ways and the
# renderings got different verdicts. TRIANGULATION-GROUPS is the artifact worth
# trusting -- it carries no labels, only (grant_id, group_id), and feeds
# pf_consistency(). SAMPLE is an adjudication queue at ~50-60% precision, not
# an answer key. See dev/build-triangulation-sample.R for which is which.
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-GROUPS.csv
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-SAMPLE.csv
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-CANDIDATES.csv
!data-dev/TRIANGULATION-GATED.csv
!data-dev/PF-TRUTH-TRIANGULATED.csv

# ---- source data (625 MB) --------------------------------------------------
inputs/*
# ... except the benchmark fixtures and the NTEE source, all small and public,
# so that a clean clone can run the 1k benchmark and rebuild data/nteev2.rda
!inputs/1k_grants_0*.csv
# ... and the e-file rebuild's equivalents. Kept alongside rather than
# replacing the line above: BASELINE-2026-08 is defined as the benchmark over
# 1k_grants_0*, so overwriting those would make the frozen reference point
# unreproducible.
!inputs/ef1k_grants_0*.csv
# ... and the v2 lift, which BASELINE-2026-10B is defined over, plus the
# independent draw that shows the lift still represents the deduplicated
# population. Same reasoning again: a frozen baseline whose population is not
# in the repository is not reproducible.
!inputs/efv2_1k_grants_0*.csv
!inputs/effresh_1k_grants_0*.csv
!inputs/nteev2-descriptions.csv
!inputs/nteev2-descriptions-tidy-format.csv
!inputs/GTDC*.xlsx

# The BMF (1.7 GB) lives in ../npmatch/data-raw and is never tracked here.
# The 990 Part III extracts (525 MB) are re-downloadable from the GT 990 lake;
# see dev/build-990-text-wide.R for the filenames.

# ---- R build / session -----------------------------------------------------
.Rproj.user/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata
*.Rproj
*.tar.gz
*.Rcheck/
/data/*.rda.bak

# ---- OS --------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini


# docs/ IS committed: GitHub Pages serves the site from main:/docs.
# Rebuild with pkgdown::build_site() and commit the result.
